<section id="how"><h2>How we rank + Sources</h2><div class="card"><p class="note" style="margin:0 0 6px">Independent boards first; overlapping error ranges count as tied.</p>
<details><summary>How we rank</summary><ul class="in"><li><b>Ties:</b> on boards with error ranges, rank = 1 + models whose whole range sits above (LMArena’s rule), so overlaps show “=”. Boards with no ranges are ranked by value only and called “close race” when the gap is small.</li>
<li><b>Tags:</b> Confirmed = official or independent source · Vendor says / Authors report = the company’s or authors’ own account · Outlet reports = one outlet’s reporting, not yet officially confirmed · Too close to call = tied within ranges.</li>
<li><b>Jobs:</b> each pick keeps its own as-of date and is carried forward until its board updates. Independent boards first (AA = Artificial Analysis, Vals, LMArena, Epoch, Scale, ARC Prize). Harnesses, scales and method versions are never mixed.</li>
<li><b>Not shown today:</b> two benchmark rows held as low priority (Mercury 3 on the Vals Index; d1-ultra on ClaimBench).</li></ul></details>
